PostgreSQL migrations use the application DATABASE_URL setting, or a connection
supplied through Alembic Config.attributes["connection"] for isolated tests.

0001 freezes the original 16-table ORM schema.
0002 adds exact numerics, stable observation keys, lineage constraints, and
database-backed raw/normalized snapshots and quarantine dispositions.
0003 separates acquisition from replay processing, adds bounded batch history,
and records request metadata and originating run references.

Run python -m alembic upgrade head from the repository root.
Do not use create_all for managed databases. Existing starter databases must be
verified against revision 0001 before stamping that revision and upgrading.
Downgrade 0002 refuses to discard captured evidence or numeric precision.